# Elevator Controller using Verilog

## Description

This project implements a 4-floor elevator controller using Verilog HDL.

The elevator can move between four floors:

    Floor 1
    Floor 2
    Floor 3
    Floor 4

The controller receives floor requests and moves the elevator
to the requested floor.

## Inputs

    clk       : Clock signal
    reset     : Active-high reset
    request   : Requested floor (2-bit)
    req_valid : Indicates a valid floor request

## Outputs

    motor_up   : Elevator moves upward
    motor_down : Elevator moves downward
    door_open  : Door open indicator
    floor      : Current floor

## Floor Encoding

    2'b00 = Floor 1
    2'b01 = Floor 2
    2'b10 = Floor 3
    2'b11 = Floor 4

## Operation

Example:

    Current floor = 1
    Request       = 3

The elevator moves:

    Floor 1 -> Floor 2 -> Floor 3

Then the door opens.

## FSM States

    IDLE
    UP
    DOWN
    DOOR_OPEN

## Files

    elevator_controller.v
        Main elevator controller.

    tb_elevator_controller.v
        Testbench.

    README.md
        Project documentation.

## Simulation

Compile:

    iverilog -o elevator_tb elevator_controller.v tb_elevator_controller.v

Run:

    vvp elevator_tb
